import orchestrate as team

team.JOBS={
 'icons': '''Create ONLY dist/icons.svg. User explicitly rejects emojis and wants custom professional nautical game UI. SVG sprite with <symbol id="icon-NAME" viewBox="0 0 48 48"> for hook, floor, fish, wood, leaf, scrap, barrel, sail, palm, lantern, net, crew, help, sound, close, repair, hammer, compass. Original hand-drawn vector icons with warm realistic nautical details: timber grain, steel hook, coiled rope, green leaves. Cohesive palette dark navy #153e49, warm wood #bb8650, cream #fff2cc, muted teal #54a6a4, amber #ffbd66; 2px dark outlines, no emoji/font glyphs. Each symbol must be self-contained, have strong silhouette and work at 24px or 36px. Use actual SVG paths and shapes, never text or Unicode icon characters. No external images, CSS or dependencies, no scripts. Parent will use <svg><use href="icons.svg#icon-hook"/></svg>. Do not change any other files. No shell, git, deployment, or further agents. Return list of IDs.''',
 'hud-art': '''Create ONLY dist/graphics.css, an additional stylesheet loaded after existing style.css. User wants a real first-person raft game with bespoke UI, no emoji, no generic web dashboard feel. Restyle existing HUD selectors into polished understated nautical game interface: dark translucent navy inventory/hotbar with fine bronze/rope-inspired borders, crisp cream labels, warm amber selection indicators, subtle engraved highlights, believable wood/metal but not excessive decorative clutter. Keep screen center clear for first-person aiming. Existing classes/IDs: header .brand .brand-icon .header-right #connection .inventory .inventory>div .inventory b .inventory strong .inventory small .goal .progress .bottom .tools .tools button .tools button.selected .tools button>span .controls #recipes #recipes button #recipes button.active #aimHint #toast .welcome-card .eyebrow .pills .primary .secondary dialog #roomDisplay. Engine adds body.playing at start, #crosshair and #resumeHint exist. Another worker produces icons.svg and parent swaps icon span content to SVG; style .icon {width:28px;height:28px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle} .tools .icon etc. Make #crosshair a clean four-tick reticle with 2px center, no emoji. Add .durability-meter etc for optional durability: #durability at left lower above hotbar, text 'HOOK CONDITION', bar .durability-track>i. Design must respect dialogs and not change pointer-events on interactive controls, maintain text at readable sizes, responsive at 1280x720 and 390x844. Avoid @import or assets. No functionality changes, no other files. No shell, git, deployments, or further agents. Return integration notes.''',
 'ocean': '''Create ONLY dist/ocean.js exporting createOcean(T) returning {mesh, update(time)}. User wants an appealing more realistic first-person Raft-inspired ocean, real gentle rocking, designs that feel like wood/metal/water rather than blocks. Build a performant THREE Mesh using PlaneGeometry rotated horizontal, ~100x100 subdivisions size 280, y average -.24. Use THREE ShaderMaterial with animated multi-frequency Gerstner-like waves (amplitudes .04-.12 to never flood floor at .2), animated normal/specular ocean highlights, deep teal to turquoise variation, thin sparse moving foam, distance fade toward sky #99dfe1. Sun direction (-15,28,12). Can use vertex + fragment GLSL with uniforms uTime, uCamera; update(time) sets time; use cameraPosition built-in. Must support THREE 0.170.0 WebGLRenderer ACES tone mapping, include <tonemapping_fragment> and <colorspace_fragment> if appropriate. Avoid huge assets, external dependencies, texture fetches, scene changes, shadow dependency. Handle fog optionally using manual distance fade. Ocean must stay legible around floating resources with no harsh flashing or camera nausea; subtle realistic motion. Aim one draw call, no new geometry per frame. Only edit ocean.js. Coordinator replaces old water init/update with your returned mesh/update. No shell, git, deployment or further agents. Return API details.''',
 'hook-model': '''Create ONLY dist/hook.js exporting createHook(T), returning THREE.Group model for a first-person held scrap hook. Coordinate contract: group centered at origin, total dimensions ~.7 wide, .8 tall, .4 deep. Hook point up, handle bottom, front toward -Z. Parent will attach group to camera around (.4,-.35,-.75) scaled appropriately. Detailed recognizable curved steel hook using CatmullRomCurve3 + TubeGeometry (steel #8ca8ac, metalness .7 roughness .3), rope-wrapped weathered wooden handle, rivets, maybe small coil/tied cord. No emojis, textures, dependencies, lights, animation loops, scene access, or external assets. A hook kids recognize, with believable materials and not a dangerous bloody weapon. MeshStandardMaterials, moderate total <=20 meshes. Parent animates casting and hand separately. Only edit hook.js. No shell, git, deployment or subagents. Return size/orientation details.'''
}
team.launch()
